For $J_{\rm nom}>0$, the relative cost overrun $\varepsilon_c$ is computed from
the paired cumulative costs using the definition in Section~\ref{sec:problem_setup}.
Geometric deviation is measured as the maximum planar distance between
time-aligned base positions,
\begin{equation}
\varepsilon_d=\max_{0\leq t\leq T} \left\|p_t^{\rm exec}-p_t^{\rm nom}\right\|_2,
\label{eq:max_planar_deviation}
\end{equation}
where $p_t$ is the base position.

